    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Uganda became independent in 1962 as a quasi-federal state built around Buganda and the other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#great-lakes">Great Lakes</a> kingdoms.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#milton-obote">Obote</a> abolished the kingdoms in 1967, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#idi-amin">Idi Amin</a>’s rule of 1971–1979 killed an estimated 100,000 or more people.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#yoweri-museveni">Yoweri Museveni</a>, in power since 1986, restored order and growth and brought back the kingdoms as cultural institutions in 1993.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Rwandan exiles who fought in Museveni’s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#national-resistance-army">National Resistance Army</a>, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#paul-kagame">Paul Kagame</a>, went on to lead the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rwandan-patriotic-front">Rwandan Patriotic Front</a>, which invaded Rwanda from Uganda in 1990.</p></aside>
    </section>

